<p>hey mrpufferfish, I can't provide you with your long-desired green light, nor am I a proper critter, but you should still take my feedback to heart. So let's dig in</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Right now your article is just a bit tasteless and dull, having no story or substance, there's nothing that pops out in any way, and the story has several plot holes</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A group of people wanted to create a breakaway civilisation, duo to political difficulties, and considering they didn't have much,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If they remained poor and homeless (which is what I'm guessing your implying), how were they able to advance or have the supplies for space travel? Within this timeline of the foundation, was space travel commonplace, hence the group just casually flying to space, but if so, why did they make their home out of trash, Why didn't the society wait on earth, what did they gain from travelling to space that had a larger benefit to them more than staying on earth? the motives of your group are just confusing, and strange?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>breakaway civilisation, duo to political difficulties,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What were these political struggles? Rich against the poor? Different belief and society? You have an excellent opportunity where you could relate with your audience, where they sympathise with your characters, the group's treatment by the rest of the world&#8230; Outcasts, loners.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the project was abandoned, the rest of the space station was built anonymously.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What does this add to the foundation and the law it carries, self-building trash? Like I've said before your idea doesn't add much to the story of the site, although, I do believe this does have heaps of potential behind it, and it could be turned into something truly great. Diary entries, discovery logs and a dark secret hidden just below a fake facade it's really your decision, once you've tidy up the plot holes and my question, and just dig a little deeper you could have a really good article</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Good luck<br />
Dr G</strong></p>

