<p>As I said, I'm having trouble with the narrative, and so, some plot holes are to be expected.</p>
<p>Thank you for pointing out the plot holes, I will now try to answer these questions as best as I can:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If they remained poor and homeless (which is what I'm guessing your implying), how were they able to advance or have the supplies for space travel?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I never said they are poor, I just said they didn't have much materials. As for how they turned wasted materials into a rocket ship and a space station module? I would like to leave that part anomalous. (Like how a group of people called &quot;Are we cool yet&quot; created a painting that causes hallucinations.)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why didn't the society wait on earth</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The group decided to wait on earth after the first module was done, hence why I wrote</p>
<blockquote>
<p>after the first module was done, the project was abandoned</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>what did they gain from travelling to space that had a larger benefit to them more than staying on earth?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>They wanted to make a society in space because, well, they didn't want to be discrimanted back on earth, in space, nobody can bother them (I didn't really know how to answer that question, you can suggest things if you want).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Within this timeline of the foundation, was space travel commonplace</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, I don't know really, I haven't thought about that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What were these political struggles?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm gonna go with the discrimination of religions and different societies.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What does this add to the foundation and the law it carries, self-building trash?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, yea, it collected space junk from near earth orbit, and built itself out of that, you can even add wasted materials to it. I don't really know what you mean by law, but I will try to add some more story elements.</p>
<p>Thank you for the critique and have a nice day!</p>
</div>
