<p>I'd say this is just setting up the rest, but that might change.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What kinds of things DO they remember that will help the Foundation and the reader figure things out?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I didn't really think about this at the time I made the decision to include that, but let's say that they remember all of the things they did BEFORE boarding the space station, like the last place they were at before those events.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why do you think they erased their memories? What clues let the Foundation and the readers figure this out actively while moving through your world?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I didn't really think about this at the time either as to why they erased their memories, as for the clues, let's say one of them said that they remember building a machine part, another saying that the last thing they remember is that they were designing something, etc.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Making SCiPs useful can be a bit of a trap.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yea, revisiting this a month later, that was a bit of a silly decision, I might just remove that part.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You've told me about your mystery (the origins and such) but not about your characters. If this is your hook, can you tell me more about them?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Could we do this in discord DMs? (just asking because I don't quite like discussing things over wikidot)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What interesting details and hints are you going to go through? Is this DNA testing and more interviews or is it more like tracking movements and looking at missing persons? What are you planning to make this mysterious but also not confusing or vague?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Considering I just got back into writing this, I don't quite have a plan yet, but I will try my best to come up with one. (also I'd say this is dna testing and more interviews)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope you have a nice day.</p>

